## 5. MVP Scope — 30-Day Execution Plan

**Non-negotiable constraint:** if a feature isn't required to make the loop *agent submits → gets scored → appears on leaderboard* work end-to-end, it's out of scope for Phase 1.

### Week 1 — Core simulation
- [ ] Next.js scaffold, Tailwind/Shadcn theme, dark-mode terminal aesthetic
- [ ] R3F canvas with a single scene: table, robotic arm (simple kinematic chain, 4-6 DOF), 3 blocks, target zone
- [ ] Rapier physics integration, fixed-timestep loop, basic collision + grasp constraint
- [ ] Manual keyboard-controlled arm (sanity check before wiring up agents)

### Week 2 — Evaluation loop
- [ ] Scoring functions: spatial accuracy (distance/orientation error to target pose), task completion (binary + partial credit), joint torque telemetry capture
- [ ] WebSocket server (can live in a Next.js API route or a small standalone Node service) implementing the state/action/result contract above
- [ ] Baseline agent (`Baseline-IK`) implemented in-repo as a reference/sanity-check agent

### Week 3 — Platform & leaderboard
- [ ] Supabase schema + RLS from Section 4.3
- [ ] GitHub OAuth login
- [ ] ELO calculation service (standard ELO update on match completion, K-factor tuned for small sample sizes)
- [ ] Leaderboard UI (sortable table, agent detail page with match history)

### Week 4 — SDK & public launch
- [ ] `vsarena` PyPI package: `Agent` base class, `run_match()`, local mock-env dry-run mode
- [ ] API key generation flow in the dashboard
- [ ] README + quickstart docs good enough for a stranger to submit an agent in <10 minutes
- [ ] Seed the leaderboard with 3 baseline agents (SmolVLA, OpenVLA-micro, Baseline-IK) so the arena isn't empty on day 1
- [ ] Public launch post (X/Reddit r/robotics/HN) — ship in public, tag NovaCoding-G

### Explicitly out of scope for MVP
- Multiple task types beyond block stacking
- Server-authoritative anti-cheat physics
- Payments/monetization (open-core split comes post-MVP once there's usage data)
- Mobile-responsive simulation view (dashboard/leaderboard should be responsive; the 3D canvas itself is desktop-first for MVP)
- Faithful Colosseum 3D reproduction (post-MVP v1.1 visual; current pit in `ArenaSet` is the stand-in)

